  "name": "manual_195f34",
  "claim": "Windows .cmd/.bat files require CRLF line endings. cmd.exe tokenises on CRLF; LF-only batch files silently fail or produce garbled output. Fix in Python: open in binary mode and join lines with '\\r\\n'. Verify: xxd my.cmd | grep -c '0d 0a' must equal line count. Git prevention: declare '*.cmd text eol=crlf' in .gitattributes. Root cause confirmed in orama-system PR #108 (gstack-brain-sync.cmd). Documented in docs/wiki/08-git-hygiene-and-branching.md.",
